Host Mesa packages and release transactions
------------------------------------------
The common Ubuntu Mesa packaging lock, build and transaction tools are imported
from yzddmr6/xiaomipad-8pro-mainline, commit a1d1cf180487ec425c471cca7ea6f2b92958d724.
File hashes and original licenses are retained in packaging/mesa/provenance.json
and the imported source files. The OnePlus transition and image integration are
maintained here; the common implementation is maintained in the source repository.

NPU runtime (packaging/npu, tools/build-npu.py): Qualcomm FastRPC from
https://github.com/qualcomm/fastrpc (BSD-3-Clause, see upstream LICENSE.txt);
llama.cpp from https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp (MIT); one build-only CMake patch removes compiler/linker command notes before SWIV generation. Fixed revisions and archive identities are in packaging/npu/sources.json.
The local hybrid demo and packaging are MIT. Hexagon SDK is a build-time input
from snapdragon-toolchain/hexagon-sdk; it is not included in runtime packages.
Qwen3-0.6B weights are Apache-2.0 (Qwen team), converted to GGUF by Unsloth.
Stock DSP shells and libraries are included under firmware/npu with source identities.
They are Qualcomm/vendor property; no redistribution permission has been obtained,
and they will be removed upon request from the rights holder.
